---
import BaseLayout from '../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageWrapper from '../components/layout/PageWrapper.astro';
import Container from '../components/ui/Container.astro';
import Link from '../components/ui/Link.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';

const canonicalUrl = new URL('/privacy/', SITE.siteUrl).toString();
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy and Cookies"
  description="How jetsanchez.com handles analytics, cookies, browser storage, hosting data, and the local-first Egregore experience."
  canonicalURL={canonicalUrl}
>
  <PageWrapper spacing="default">
    <Container size="md">
      <article class="mx-auto max-w-[var(--container-3xl)] space-y-xl">
        <header class="space-y-s">
          <h1 class="text-5xl font-bold leading-tight text-text-primary">
            Privacy and Cookies
          </h1>
          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-text-tertiary">
            Effective August 26, 2026
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            This notice explains what happens to information when you visit
            jetsanchez.com, including which technologies use cookies and which
            keep data only in your browser.
          </p>
        </header>

        <section aria-labelledby="owner" class="space-y-s">
          <h2 id="owner" class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-primary">
            Who runs this site
          </h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            This is the personal website of {SITE.author}. Questions or privacy
            requests can be sent to
            <Link href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} variant="primary">
              {SITE.email}
            </Link>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="hosting" class="space-y-s">
          <h2 id="hosting" class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-primary">
            Hosting and media delivery
          </h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Vercel hosts and delivers this site. When your browser requests a
            page or asset, Vercel may process ordinary request information such
            as the IP address, requested URL, timestamp, browser or device
            details, and security or diagnostic data needed to deliver and
            protect the service.
          </p>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Some public images and other media are served from Vercel Blob.
            These published assets use stable, immutable media URLs, so a
            request may go directly to Vercel's public Blob delivery network.
            They are site content, not files submitted by visitors. See the
            <Link
              href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-notice"
              variant="primary"
              external
            >
              Vercel Privacy Notice
            </Link>
            and
            <Link
              href="https://vercel.com/docs/vercel-blob"
              variant="primary"
              external
            >
              Vercel Blob documentation
            </Link>
            for provider information.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="analytics" class="space-y-s">
          <h2 id="analytics" class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-primary">
            Analytics
          </h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Google Analytics 4 (GA4) is included only in an explicit Vercel
            production deployment. Local development, local previews, CI, and
            Vercel Preview builds do not include GA4, so routine development and
            automated test traffic from those environments is excluded at
            source.
          </p>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            On a production request, Vercel supplies an approximate request
            country. This site uses that value only to assign a coarse strict or
            standard analytics policy. The privacy-control layer persists only
            that coarse policy and the visitor's GA preference, not the IP
            address, city, or coordinates. Vercel may still process ordinary
            request data as described under Hosting and media delivery.
          </p>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            The strict policy applies conservatively to the EEA, the UK,
            Switzerland, and requests whose country is unknown or missing. This
            is a site risk policy, not a legal-status determination. Under the
            strict policy, GA4 does not initialize unless the visitor chooses
            Allow.
          </p>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Under the standard policy, GA4 starts normally and remains subject
            to the site's Privacy settings. Choosing Reject stops GA4 and
            suppresses future analytics measurement from that browser profile;
            choosing Allow enables it. These choices do not identify a physical
            device or automatically recognize this Mac.
          </p>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            When GA4 is active, this site sends page location, path, and title
            for page-view measurement. GA4 may also receive or derive
            information such as visit and interaction timing, referring or
            campaign information, approximate location, and browser,
            operating-system, and device categories. Google Analytics uses
            identifiers and may set analytics cookies to distinguish browsers
            and sessions.
          </p>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            The existing <code>?analytics=off</code> and
            <code>?analytics=on</code> URL controls remain an optional, persistent
            production browser-profile fallback. They apply to that browser profile
            rather than identifying or filtering a physical device.
          </p>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            More information is available in the
            <Link
              href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
              variant="primary"
              external
            >
              Google Privacy Policy
            </Link>
            and Google's
            <Link
              href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/cookies"
              variant="primary"
              external
            >
              explanation of analytics cookies
            </Link>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="browser-storage" class="space-y-s">
          <h2 id="browser-storage" class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-primary">
            Cookies and browser storage
          </h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Cookies are small values sent with web requests. <code
              >localStorage</code
            >,
            <code>sessionStorage</code>, Cache Storage, and in-memory state are
            separate browser technologies; they are not cookies and are not
            automatically sent with every request.
          </p>
          <dl
            class="divide-y divide-border-default rounded-xl border border-border-default bg-bg-subtle"
          >
            <div class="grid gap-2xs p-s sm:grid-cols-[10rem_1fr] sm:gap-s">
              <dt class="font-semibold text-text-primary">Analytics cookies</dt>
              <dd class="leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
                When GA4 is active, it may use cookies for visit and session
                measurement. The site's privacy controls use first-party browser
                storage to remember only the coarse analytics policy and the
                visitor's GA preference across pages in that browser profile.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div class="grid gap-2xs p-s sm:grid-cols-[10rem_1fr] sm:gap-s">
              <dt class="font-semibold text-text-primary">Theme</dt>
              <dd class="leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
                The light or dark theme choice is stored as <code>theme</code> in
                <code>localStorage</code> so it persists in the browser.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div class="grid gap-2xs p-s sm:grid-cols-[10rem_1fr] sm:gap-s">
              <dt class="font-semibold text-text-primary">
                Liquid Glass navigation
              </dt>
              <dd class="leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
                The mobile Liquid Glass dock's discovered and open-or-closed
                state is stored in <code>sessionStorage</code> for the current tab
                session.
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div class="grid gap-2xs p-s sm:grid-cols-[10rem_1fr] sm:gap-s">
              <dt class="font-semibold text-text-primary">Egregore</dt>
              <dd class="leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
                The local model may use browser Cache Storage, while prompts and
                conversation turns use in-memory session state. Details and
                controls are below.
              </dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="egregore" class="space-y-s">
          <h2 id="egregore" class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-primary">
            Egregore
          </h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Egregore is a local-first assistant. Opening its page does not
            download or start the model. After you check compatibility, only the
            explicit “Load Egregore” action starts the model download and
            browser runtime.
          </p>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            The pinned model is about 2 GB and is downloaded directly from
            Hugging Face. When supported, it is kept in this browser's Cache
            Storage for reuse. The compatibility check may ask the browser for a
            storage estimate to warn when the reported available space may be
            low; the site does not receive the estimate. If Cache Storage is
            unavailable, the interface explains that the model will be loaded
            without being cached.
          </p>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Questions, assembled prompts, generated responses, and conversation
            turns stay in this browser's current session. Model generation runs
            locally, and there is no cloud conversation history. Ordinary
            hosting and production analytics requests for the Egregore page
            remain subject to the sections above, and the model host receives
            the download request when you choose to load it.
          </p>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            “New session” clears the current conversation. “Unload” releases the
            active runtime but retains a cached model for faster reuse. When a
            model is cached, the “Remove downloaded model” control in Egregore
            removes its current Cache Storage entry after confirmation. Browser
            site-data controls can also remove stored site data.
          </p>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            See the
            <Link href="/licenses/egregore/" variant="primary">
              Egregore model and open-source licenses
            </Link>
            for the exact model, runtime, and software notices.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="external-links" class="space-y-s">
          <h2 id="external-links" class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-primary">
            External links
          </h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Links to third-party websites, profiles, papers, and source material
            take you to services with their own privacy practices. This notice
            does not control what those services collect after you follow a
            link.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="retention" class="space-y-s">
          <h2 id="retention" class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-primary">
            Retention
          </h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Analytics information is retained according to the configured GA4
            property settings and only for as long as reasonably needed to
            understand site use, investigate unusual traffic, and maintain the
            site. Hosting and delivery providers keep request or security data
            under their own retention policies. Messages you choose to send by
            email may be kept as needed to reply and maintain an appropriate
            record of the exchange.
          </p>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Browser-held data follows a different lifecycle: the theme remains
            until changed or cleared, the Liquid Glass session state normally
            ends with the tab session, and the Egregore model remains until you
            remove it, clear site data, or the browser evicts it. Egregore
            conversation turns are not saved as cloud history.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="rights" class="space-y-s">
          <h2 id="rights" class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-primary">
            Your choices and rights
          </h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            You can clear or block cookies and other site data in your browser,
            use the site's production analytics controls (including the
            browser-profile fallback described above), remove the Egregore
            model, and choose not to follow external links. Blocking storage may
            stop preferences or local-first features from working as intended.
          </p>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            Depending on where you live, you may have rights to ask about,
            access, correct, delete, restrict, or object to processing of your
            personal information. Contact
            <Link href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} variant="primary">
              {SITE.email}
            </Link>
            with enough detail to understand and respond to the request. For information
            controlled by Google or Vercel, use the rights and contact routes in their
            privacy notices.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="changes" class="space-y-s">
          <h2 id="changes" class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-primary">
            Changes to this notice
          </h2>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
            This notice may change when the site's services or data practices
            change. The effective date at the top will be updated when a revised
            notice is published.
          </p>
        </section>
      </article>
    </Container>
  </PageWrapper>
</BaseLayout>
